  "final_text": "The raw API check didn't work. The alerting endpoint returned 401 for this key, while the status endpoint worked without auth. The MCP tools already confirmed the rule's name, enabled state, and schedule, so I'll stop here and report that the parameters weren't independently re-read.\n\nBoth items are in place in Kibana (`localhost:15601`).\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-ac334308 Web logs overview`**\n- Six panels, all on the `Kibana Sample Data Logs` data view:\n  - Total requests (count)\n  - Unique client IPs\n  - Average response size (bytes)\n  - Requests over time (line, by `timestamp`)\n  - Requests by response code (bar, by `response.keyword`)\n  - Top countries by requests (bar, by `geo.dest`)\n- Time range is set to Sep 2026 through Dec 2026, which covers the sample data. The default of last 7 days would show almost nothing.\n- URL: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-ac334308-web-logs-overview-5c0909e18b2f\n\n**Alert rule: `EFF-ac334308 5xx spike`**\n- Enabled, type `.es-query`, runs every 1m.\n- Counts documents where `response.keyword` matches `5*` in the last 5 minutes, and fires when the count is greater than 10.\n- Rule ID: `dc5cf507-0ceb-4289-b0b0-fadef7d7b1a4`. Status is \"pending\" because it hasn't run yet.\n\n**What I found in the data**\n- 14,074 requests from 1,001 distinct IPs, with timestamps from 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03.\n- `response` has only three values: 200 (12,832), 404 (801), and 503 (441). So the only 5xx code present is 503.\n\n**Things to know**\n- The sample timestamps run into the future relative to today (2026-10-12). Because the rule looks at the last 5 minutes, it will only fire if new 5xx events arrive in real time. It won't fire on the historical data.\n- I didn't re-read the rule's stored parameters, because the raw alerting API returned 401 for the key. The threshold, window, and query were set in the create call, but I haven't confirmed them against the stored object.",
